    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1058">

                <pb facs="0976" n="964" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg964"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760d.61/234: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Helsinki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-10-10T11:00:00+02:00">October 10,
                            1939—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 10—7:22 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>232. Press today reports departure for Moscow last night of Minister Paasikivi as
                    special envoy accompanied by Colonel Paasonen the President’s<anchor n="35"
                        xml:id="d1058-f1"/> senior <hi rendition="#italic">aide-de-camp</hi> as
                    military expert and Mr. Nykopp of the Foreign Office as secretary. Evidence of
                    military preparations on extensive scale increasingly apparent.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1058-f1" n="35" xml:id="d1058-f1-content">
